scenario: "Any future consumer needing the MST edge struct in Cython (e.g. a new HDBSCAN routine) must either duplicate the ctypedef or bounce through Python; the mutual-reachability computation is now split between `_reachability.pyx` (dense/sparse over precomputed distances) and `_linkage.pyx` (implicit inside prims), so behavior changes to core-distance semantics must be duplicated across two files."
contract: `MST_edge_t` must be published from a pxd (either `_linkage.pxd` or `_tree.pxd`) if it is part of the cross-module contract, and the mutual-reachability arithmetic must live in one module — either fully inside `_reachability.pyx` (called from prims) or with a documented rationale for the intentional inlining.
